 "description": "Measure one ACTUAL photograph. Example shape: {\"face\":\"front\",\"image_base64\":\"<complete actual image bytes>\"}. Ask front/back BEFORE calling if unknown. Exactly one user-provided public HTTPS image URL (port 443) or complete base64 source, never both. Never decode, repair or re-encode bytes yourself; never invent, shorten or rewrite base64; pass it verbatim, including an image data-URL prefix or whitespace (service normalizes). If chat attachment cannot be forwarded, send user to https://centeringlab.com/. card_size standard=63\u00d788 mm including Japanese Pok\u00e9mon; small=59\u00d786 mm including Yu-Gi-Oh!, not inferred from language. Request a whole card flat from above on dark surface; if sleeved/toploader or tilted, recommend a retake first. Borderless: suggest back/manual site. API photos reach server memory; site stays local. needs-review/failed gives ceilings=null: retake or adjust manually, no grade prediction. Inspect status/code even on HTTP 200; respect Retry-After.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
